# AI Knowledge Tree maintenance

- Keep user workflows simple, lightweight and automatic. Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- After completing changes, run relevant checks (`npm test` for code), update README when behavior changes, and commit and push to the existing origin.
- This synchronization preference applies to all subsequent edits in this project unless the user overrides it.
- Inspect the working tree first. Preserve unrelated user changes and never force-push or discard work to resolve a conflict.
- Never commit API keys, real conversations, exported personal notes, browser profiles, logs or temporary backups.
- Do not make real paid model calls in automated tests. Use mock providers.
- Report validation limits and any authentication or push failure honestly.
